  "res": {
   "attrs": {
    "redundancy": "1+1",
    "redundancy-note": "1+1 - mx2010 hardware guide, \"MX2010 Component Redundancy\": the host subsystem is a combined Control Board and Routing Engine (CB-RE); with two fitted one is primary and the other backup, and the backup takes over if the primary or any part of it fails. Fabric is NOT on this card on this chassis - it is on the eight SFBs, see `sfbs`"
   },
   "description": "CB-RE slots 0 and 1 at the ends of the upper cage",
   "index-origin": 0,
   "role": "service",
   "term": "Slot"
  },
  "sfbs": {
   "attrs": {
    "redundancy": "n+1",
    "redundancy-note": "n+1 - mx2010 hardware guide, \"MX2000-SFB-S Switch Fabric Board Description\": 6 Tbps with a minimum of seven SFBs fitted, and an eighth recommended for N+1. The same entry gives the slot count these eight bays come from - up to eight SFBs in an MX2000 - and its redundancy row says seven are needed for line rate and fewer degrades forwarding. The fabric is all-active, so the spare is a working plane. RECORDED AS THE GUIDE WRITES IT: seven-plus-one would be an arithmetic reading of two sentences and the guide itself says N+1"
   },
   "description": "Switch Fabric Board slots SFB 0-7",
   "index-origin": 0,
   "role": "service",
   "term": "Slot"
  }
